# Terraform Standards

Use `scripts/cloud/run_terraform.ps1`; never run raw Terraform inside a stack dir.

## Stacks

- `infra/terraform/bootstrap/`: state bucket, locks, budget; local state by design.
- `infra/terraform/`: platform for **dev/prod** (cloud only — not local Docker).
  Backend: `envs/<env>.backend.hcl`; vars: `envs/<env>.tfvars`.

## Platform Modules

`s3`, `kafka` (MSK + topics + lag alarms), `emr`, `redshift` (Serverless + Spectrum),
`mwaa` (optional), `streamlit` (optional App Runner).

## Rules

- Tags: `Project`, `Environment`, `Team` (+ `Layer` where useful).
- Variables for non-defaults; outputs for scripts/DAGs/runbooks.
- One platform stack for dev and prod — do not revive lean/redshift-dev stacks.
- Do not commit `.terraform/`, `*.tfstate*`, or real `*.tfvars`.

## Commands

```powershell
.\scripts\cloud\run_terraform.ps1 -Stack platform -Env dev -Action validate
.\scripts\cloud\run_terraform.ps1 -Stack platform -Env prod -Action plan
.\scripts\cloud\deploy_platform.ps1 -Env dev
```

Local laptop infra is Docker Compose on `local-testing-version`, not Terraform.
